[Music]  dates on food guide us when we go  shopping  but many people are confused about what  use by and best before mean  one indicates the last day a product is  safe to eat  the other that the food can be consumed  but is past its best  as part of the farm to fork strategy the  european commission is looking into new  date marking rules  less than half of consumers understand  the difference between used by and best  before this has very tangible  consequences 10 of europe's food waste  is due to a lack of understanding of  date marking  we check out how major retailers and  consumer organizations are dealing with  this  [Music]  test asha the oldest consumer  association in belgium points out that  sometimes both best before and used by  are used on the same kind of products  this can be misleading  as a consumer when you see these two  products that look similar  and you see that they use different date  markers it obviously adds confusion  you wonder why one is considered highly  perishable and not the other  in reality this is a second issue that  adds to the confusion  how date marking is managed by food  business operators along the supply  chain can also have an impact on food  waste  here products pass their best before  date are being sold at a lower price  given to charities or even used to  produce energy through natural processes  we lower the price of products that are  close to their use by date with yellow  promotional labels  then we give the products that don't  sell to charities and then they'll be  distributed to people who need them  the products that are unfit for  consumption are also recycled and made  into green energy  to improve the understanding and use of  date marking for everyone the european  commission has launched an impact study  and requested scientific advice from the  european food safety authority  consumer organizations like the belgian  test asha want to join the initiative  [Music]  we're very happy that the european  commission is taking up this issue  an impact study has been carried out and  there will be a public consultation  which we will obviously take part in  the idea is to follow as closely as  possible any proposals that will be put  on the table to be sure that they meet  consumer expectations in terms of  clarity and understanding  let's head to france to discover an  initiative helping to reduce food waste  too good to go is an app that connects  consumers with restaurants and shops  where you can buy unsold food for less  the company also launched a campaign  with several major brands  its goal is to encourage people to use  their senses when considering food and  the best before date  [Music]  we've worked with producers on labels to  create icons that encourage consumers to  trust their senses  the icons represent the sense of sight  smell and taste and are on products with  a best before date  it makes the date more understandable  and helps consumers trust their senses  before throwing away a product that is  past its best before date  ensuring better labeling and helping  consumers make sustainable food choices  are part of the farmed fork strategy  action plan the european commission aims  to present a new set of rules on date  marking by the end of 2022  [Music]

